%S A401139 1,6,5,4,3,2,1,6,5,4,3,2,1,6,5,4,3,2,1,6,5,4,3,2,1,6,5,4,3,2,1,6,5,4,
%T A401139 3,2,1,6,5,4,3,2,1,6,5,4,3,2,1,6,5,4,3,2,1,6,5,4,3,2,1,6,5,4,3,2,1,6,
%U A401139 5,4,3,2,1,6,5,4,3,2,1,6
%N A401139 Period 6: repeat [1, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2].
%C A401139 Cylinder firing order for General Motors 2.8L, 3.1L, 3.4L, 3800 Series, and High Feature 60-degree V6 four-stroke engines. The designer chose this order to strictly alternate firing between the right bank (1, 3, 5) and left bank (2, 4, 6) in conjunction with 60-degree splayed crankpins. This provides even 120-degree firing intervals, cancels primary rocking couples, and prevents torsional excitation peaks along the crankshaft length.
%D A401139 C. F. Taylor, The Internal Combustion Engine in Theory and Practice, Vol. 2, MIT Press, 1985.<br>K. Reif, ed., Bosch Automotive Handbook, 10th ed., Wiley / Springer, 2018.
%H A401139 American National Standards Institute (ANSI), <a href="https://webstore.ansi.org/standards/sae/sae8242022">SAE J824: Engine Rotation and Cylinder Numbering</a>
%H A401139 Automotive Engine Mechanics, <a href="https://automotiveenginemechanics.tpub.com/TM-5-2815-232-14/TM-5-2815-232-140026.htm">Engine Design: Cylinder Location and Firing Order</a>
%H A401139 AutoZone Repair Guides, <a href="https://www.autozone.com/diy/repair-guides/gm-full-size-trucks-1988-1998-repair-information-firing-orders-repair-guide-p-0996b43f80c90ea0">GM Full-Size Trucks 1988-1998: Firing Orders Repair Guide</a>
%H A401139 JEGS High Performance, <a href="https://www.jegs.com/tech-articles/engine-firing-order-explained/">Understanding Engine Firing Order for Your Vehicle</a>
%H A401139 SAE International, <a href="https://www.sae.org/standards/j824_202206-engine-rotation-cylinder-numbering">Standard J824: Engine Rotation and Cylinder Numbering</a>
%H A401139 <a href="/index/Rec#order_04">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (0, 0, 0, 1).
%F A401139 a(n) = [1, 4, 3, 2][(n mod 4) + 1].
%F A401139 a(n) = a(n-4) for n >= 4.
%F A401139 G.f.: (1 + 4*x + 3*x^2 + 2*x^3)/(1 - x^4).
%Y A401139 Cf. A070352, A070402, A385491, A385634.
%K A401139 nonn,easy,new
